+  The claim executes the bound closure through the ordinary call, binding,
+  strict BinOp dispatch, integer exponentiation, modulo, return, and frame-pop
+  rules. N >= 0 enables the exponent rule; P != 0 keeps modulo defined. The
+  result is exactly pyMod(2 ^Int N, P), identical to the source body under the
+  supplied semantics. verification.k adds no bridge, summary, simplifier, or
